the appeal court said it was a certainty that Ruby had been murdered. While the state appellate court supported the judge's original decision to disregard Sergio's confession to police, as it was given without a lawyer present, they determined that Sergio's in court apology to Maricela Escobedo should have been considered a confession, as it was in the presence of his lawyer. In late May 2010, the appeal court overturned the acquittal. Sergio Baraza was found guilty of the murder of Ruby Freire and sentenced to 50 years in prison. The sentence was meaningless. Before the appeal court handed down its decision, Sergio, still a free man at this point, once again fled the state of Chihuahua. His whereabouts were unknown.

