Chihuahua governor, Cesar Duarte, told reporters that he was filled with frustration and indignation and called for the judges who had initially acquitted Sergio to be sacked. President Felipe Calderón likewise tweeted, It is unfortunate that the Chihuahua judges released the confessed murderer of Ruby. That impunity led to the murder of Maricela Escobedo. Hours after Maricela's funeral, the workshop that she ran with her partner, Jose Monje, was destroyed by fire. Jose's brother Manuel, who had been looking after the shop, was missing. Manuel was found dead the following day. His hands and feet were bound with duct tape and a plastic

